35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The station block argued over a broken latch! And the complaint log shows one house is really unhappy.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The bin house smelled terrible in summer, and the supervised mornings take about fifty minutes each.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,Filing for a build takes four months and five signatures. Supervised mornings are a small time commitment per person.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Some of our frontages are too narrow for a bay, and the same house has been complaining the most.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"A shelter is expensive, though there is a subsidy. We also spend thirty-four thousand yen yearly on basic maintenance.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, if one house is unhappy, we definitely shouldn't leave the bins where they are.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"But if the bin house smells, maybe a permanent structure isn't the answer for our noses.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"The administrative burden of changing sites frequently is high, according to the clerk's requirements.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,But is it fair to keep it in one spot if that spot is too small or annoying?,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,We must be careful. A permanent build could cost over a hundred thousand yen even with the subsidy.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,I just don't want us to start arguing about who cleans the latch like the other block did.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Asuka, do you think the supervised mornings would be too stressful for the neighbors?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"The time is low, but the residents' meeting suggests people won't actually enforce the rules on each other.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"If we can't enforce it and we can't build it, maybe we should just move it around?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"Moving it might avoid a large upfront cost, but we must check if the ward allows it easily.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"Let's pick something that keeps us talking and smiling, not fighting over money or smells.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree. Peace is more important than a fancy bin house that smells like old fish.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"Logically, we need to balance the ward's strict filing rules against the unfairness of a single location.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,Exactly! No one should be stuck with the bins just because they are the quietest.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,Let us look at the options now and find the path of least resistance and most fairness.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
